 Why this build exists
 ---------------------
-v0.10 MainPassGate proved the source and copy path:
-  - full-resolution main-pass specularRect selected (3840 x 2027 in the proven run)
-  - clean RGBA8 read
-  - nonzero center RGB
-  - private snapshot matched source
-
-That closed acquisition. But v0.10 still published SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR by preferring
-current/last live specular capture before the proven snapshot. The live capture is
-still selected by the older probe-candidate logic, where refmapCount alone cannot
-separate the 512x512 probe-space pass from the full-resolution main pass.
+v0.10 proved the full-resolution Firestorm main-pass specularRect and its private
+snapshot contain real material bytes. v0.11 then made that gated snapshot the
+selected SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR source, but the FX diagnostic still sampled black
+while the overlay reported the semantic bound.
+
+That isolates the failure to publication/consumption, not acquisition:
+  - source proof is nonzero
+  - snapshot proof is nonzero and matches source
+  - v0.11 source mode is GATED MAIN-PASS SNAPSHOT
+  - FX G-buffer specular RGB is black
 
 What changed
 ------------
-Only the consumer/source priority changes:
-  1. GATED MAIN-PASS SNAPSHOT is now authoritative for SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR.
-  2. DIRECT current/last Firestorm attachment is fallback only.
-  3. The overlay exposes the actual FX source near the existing snapshot line.
-
-The SSR weighting algorithm is intentionally NOT changed in this build. This keeps
-v0.11 a single proof: does the FX consume the same main-pass material payload that
-v0.10 already proved numerically?
+The gated snapshot is no longer borrowed directly as a ReShade semantic texture.
+Instead the native bridge renders/copies all four channels into a ReShade-owned
+RGBA16F target, exactly like the already-working SL_SCENE_LINEAR publication path,
+and binds that owned view as SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR.
+
+Preserved channels:
+  legacy: RGB specular color + A glossiness
+  PBR:    RGB occlusion / roughness / metallic
+
+SSR weighting is STILL unchanged. This remains a publication proof only.
 
 Install
 -------
 Native add-on package. Close Firestorm, then run SL_InstallLatest.ps1.
 Confirm the overlay title reads:
-  SL Probe Lighting v1.6.9 ... (v0.11 MainPassConsume)
+  SL Probe Lighting v1.6.10 ... (v0.12 ReShadePublish)
 
 Report
 ------
-One overlay screenshot plus one FX diagnostic screenshot:
-  - overlay must say: SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR FX source: GATED MAIN-PASS SNAPSHOT
-  - Display Mode -> G-buffer specular RGB on the same known test object
+One overlay screenshot plus Display Mode -> G-buffer specular RGB.
+Expected overlay:
+  SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR input source: GATED MAIN-PASS SNAPSHOT
+  SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR FX publication: RESHADE-OWNED COPY
+  SL_GBUFFER_SPECULAR semantic bound: YES
+
+Expected FX diagnostic:
+  G-buffer specular RGB is visibly non-black on the known test object.
 
-Do not re-run source acquisition troubleshooting unless the overlay falls back to
-DIRECT or NONE. v0.10 source proof remains authoritative.
+The Analyze button remains manual source-proof instrumentation. Pressing it is not
+required for the semantic to update and does not cause FX publication.
